---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// DRAFT SKELETON — the structure and headings are standard for a UK sole-practitioner
// site using Netlify Forms, but every [CONFIRM: …] placeholder below must be filled in
// and the whole policy reviewed by Laura before this goes live. Do not publish as-is.

const lastUpdated = '[CONFIRM: date this policy was reviewed]';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Laura Reynolds Nutrition"
  description="How Laura Reynolds Nutrition collects, uses and stores your personal data."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">How your information is collected, used and stored.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="container container-prose prose">
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        This site is run by Laura Reynolds, trading as Laura Reynolds Nutrition
        [CONFIRM: registered business name and address, and ICO registration number if
        one is held]. I am the data controller for any personal information you send
        through this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this policy, or want a copy of the information
        held about you, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@lrnutrition.co.uk">hello@lrnutrition.co.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        If you fill in the enquiry form, I collect the details you choose to give me:
        your name, your email address, your phone number if you provide one, what you
        tell me about what you are hoping to achieve, and how you heard about me.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the only personal data this website collects. There are no analytics,
        advertising or tracking cookies on this site. [CONFIRM: still true if analytics
        are added later.]
      </p>

      <h2>Why I collect it, and the lawful basis</h2>
      <p>
        I use your details for one purpose: to reply to your enquiry and, if you go on
        to work with me, to arrange and provide that coaching. The lawful basis is
        legitimate interest — responding to someone who has deliberately contacted me —
        and, once you become a client, performance of a contract.
      </p>
      <p>
        I will not add you to a mailing list, and I will not use your details for
        marketing unless you separately ask me to.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries submitted through this site are processed by Netlify, who host the
        website and pass form submissions on to me by email. Your message is then held
        in my email account, provided by [CONFIRM: email provider, e.g. Google
        Workspace]. Both act as data processors on my behalf.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not sell your data, and I do not share it with anyone else unless I am
        legally required to.
      </p>

      <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become client relationships are deleted after [CONFIRM:
        retention period, e.g. 12 months]. Client records are kept for [CONFIRM:
        retention period — check the requirements of Laura's professional body and
        insurer, which usually set a minimum].
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask me to show you what data I hold about you, correct it
        if it is wrong, delete it, or restrict how I use it. Email the address above and
        I will respond within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not happy with how I have handled your data, you can complain to the
        Information Commissioner's Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will appear on this page with a new
        "last updated" date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Prose ── */
  .prose-section {
    padding-block: var(--section-y);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    color: var(--brown);
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .prose h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--coral-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Draft placeholders are deliberately loud — they must not reach production
     unnoticed. Styled by content, so they disappear once the text is filled in. */
  .meta {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    background-color: var(--blush-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--blush);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
